-- =====================================================================
-- Session 142 — Matt 12 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 12's extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2), S132 (Matt 3), S133 (Matt 4),
-- S134 (Matt 5), S135 (Matt 6), S137 (Matt 7-8 paired), S138 (Matt 9),
-- S139 (Matt 10), and S140 (Matt 11) extras-tier coverage. Single
-- chapter migration — Matt 12 is the Shabbat-controversies sequence
-- with three framework-major moments landing in one chapter (the
-- Shabbat-controversies with the *Son of Adam is Lord even of the
-- Shabbat* declaration; the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 42:1-4 servant-citation
-- as the longest Tanakh-quotation in Matthew; the Beelzebul-dismantling
-- with the blasphemy-against-the-Ruach HaKodesh (Holy Spirit) warning
-- as the gospel''s most load-bearing diagnostic-end-point passage),
-- plus the dense secondary architecture (tree-by-fruit and idle-words
-- at vv.33-37, the sign-of-Yonah resurrection-pre-announcement and the
-- greater-than-Yonah / greater-than-Shelomoh stature-claims at vv.38-42,
-- the unclean-spirit-returning empty-house parable at vv.43-45, and the
-- kingdom-family kinship-redefinition at vv.46-50 by the same *will of
-- my Father* criterion as Matt 7:21).
--
-- Matt 12 reading-target: the chapter walks the rejection-trajectory
-- hardening into the murder-conspiracy at v.14 with the King''s self-
-- disclosure deepening through the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 42 servant-
-- citation, the Beelzebul-dismantling-and-blasphemy-against-the-Ruach
-- warning, the sign-of-Yonah resurrection-credential pre-announcement,
-- and the kinship-redefinition closing the chapter on the same heart-
-- Torah criterion as the kingdom-entry-statement at Matt 7:21. The
-- extras-library carries multiple direct framework-bearing anchors:
-- Jubilees 2 and 50 on the Shabbat-substance with 1 Maccabees 2 on
-- the life-saving-override; Sirach 35 + Tobit 4 on mercy-as-true-
-- offering for the second Hosea 6:6 citation; Wisdom of Solomon 5
-- and 1 Enoch 95 on the eschatological-reversal of the system''s-
-- condemned-righteous; 1 Enoch 49 and 62 on the Spirit-anointed Elect
-- One for the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 42 servant-citation; Sirach 4 and 35
-- on compassion-on-the-bruised for the bruised-reed mercy-substance;
-- 1 Enoch 10 / 54 and Jubilees 10 on the binding-of-the-watchers as
-- typological-anchor for the binding-the-strong-man at Matt 12:29;
-- Jubilees 15, 1 Enoch 65, and Wisdom of Solomon 12 on the no-
-- forgiveness-for-the-hardened-disposition for the blasphemy-against-
-- the-Ruach warning; Sirach 27 and Wisdom of Solomon 1 on the tongue-
-- as-trial-of-the-heart for the tree-by-fruit / idle-words frame;
-- Wisdom of Solomon 16 + 1 Enoch 51 + Jubilees 23 on resurrection-
-- from-Sheol for the sign-of-Yonah substance; 2 Esdras 7 and Jubilees 1
-- on the evil-heart-needing-new-heart-cleansing for the empty-house
-- parable; and Wisdom of Solomon 2 + Sirach 4 + Jubilees 1 on the
-- children-of-Elohim-by-doing-the-Father''s-will architecture for the
-- kinship-redefinition.
--
-- Eleven Hebrew-library threads track the chapter''s framework moves at
-- the restoration-not-innovation register:
--   * The Shabbat as covenant-sign and protected-day with life-saving-
--     defense override at vv.1-8 — Jubilees 2:17-21 and Jubilees 50:8
--     (the angels-of-the-presence and angels-of-sanctification keeping
--     Shabbat with Yashar''el / the wisdom-stream''s Shabbat-substance
--     architecture); 1 Maccabees 2:41 (the Maccabean Shabbat-defense
--     decision documenting that life-saving-overrides-Shabbat-
--     restriction was the operative-principle in the Second Temple
--     period at the wisdom-stream register).
--   * Mercy-as-true-offering and alms-as-deliverance-from-death at v.7
--     (the second Hosea 6:6 citation) — Sirach 35:1-3 (he that keepeth
--     the law bringeth offerings enough); Sirach 34:18 (the sacrifice
--     of a thing wrongfully gotten is rejected); Tobit 4:7-11 (alms
--     doth deliver from death).
--   * Eschatological-reversal of the system-rejecting-the-righteous at
--     v.14 — Wisdom of Solomon 5:1-5 (the righteous stands in great
--     boldness before the face of such as have afflicted him); 1 Enoch
--     95:7 (woe to you who pronounce the cursing word against the
--     righteous).
--   * Spirit-anointed Elect-One with the spirit of wisdom on the Son
--     at vv.18-21 — 1 Enoch 49:1-3 (the Elect-One carries the spirit
--     of wisdom and the spirit of those who have fallen asleep in
--     righteousness); 1 Enoch 62:2 (the spirit of righteousness was
--     poured out upon him).
--   * Compassion-on-the-bruised and the cry-of-the-widow-and-orphan at
--     v.20 — Sirach 4:1-4 (despise not the supplication of the
--     afflicted); Sirach 35:13-14 (he will not despise the supplication
--     of the fatherless; nor the widow, when she poureth out her
--     complaint).
--   * The binding-of-the-watchers as typological-anchor for binding-
--     the-strong-man at vv.28-29 — 1 Enoch 10:4-5 (bind Azazel hand
--     and foot ... cover him with darkness); 1 Enoch 54:5 (Azazel and
--     his hosts cast into the burning furnace at the great-day); Jubilees
--     10:11 (the binding of nine-tenths of the wicked spirits with
--     Mastema''s allowance).
--   * No-forgiveness-for-the-hardened-disposition at vv.31-32 — Jubilees
--     15:33-34 (no forgiveness or pardon for the deliberate covenant-
--     rejection); 1 Enoch 65:11 (no place of repentance for those who
--     have witnessed the sin and hardened); Wisdom of Solomon 12:10
--     (thou gavest them place of repentance, not being ignorant that
--     their malice was bred in them, and that their cogitation would
--     never be changed).
--   * Tongue-as-trial-of-the-heart and words-as-fruit-of-the-tree at
--     vv.33-37 — Sirach 27:6-7 (the fruit declareth if the tree have
--     been dressed; so is the utterance of a conceit in the heart of
--     man — THE strongest extras-tier verbal-anchor for Matt 12:33-35);
--     Wisdom of Solomon 1:8-11 (no unrighteous talk shall pass
--     undiscovered ... a mouth that belieth slayeth the soul).
--   * Resurrection-from-Sheol substance for the sign-of-Yonah at vv.38-42
--     — Wisdom of Solomon 16:13 (thou leadest to the gates of Sheol,
--     and bringest up again); 1 Enoch 51:1 (the earth also give back ...
--     Sheol also shall give back); Jubilees 23:30 (the Lord will heal
--     His servants, And they shall rise up).
--   * The evil-heart-inherited-from-Adam needing the new-heart-cleansing
--     for the empty-house at vv.43-45 — 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:48 (O Adam,
--     what hast thou done?); 2 Esdras 7:118-119 (the wisdom-stream''s
--     architecture of the inherited-evil-heart that cannot be overcome
--     without the new-heart); Jubilees 1:23 (I shall create in them a
--     holy spirit, and I shall cleanse them — the new-heart internal-
--     replacement the empty-house lacks).
--   * Children-of-Elohim-by-doing-the-Father''s-will at vv.46-50 —
--     Wisdom of Solomon 2:13-18 (he professeth to have the knowledge
--     of Elohim ... if the just man be the son of Elohim, he will help
--     him); Sirach 4:10 (be as a father unto the fatherless ... so
--     shalt thou be as the son of the most High); Jubilees 1:24 (their
--     souls will cleave to Me and to all My commandments, and they will
--     fulfil My commandments, and I shall be their Father and they
--     will be My children).
--
-- Editions used at S142: Apocrypha KJV 1611 (`apocrypha` — Sirach /
-- Ecclesiasticus, Wisdom of Solomon, Tobit, 1 Maccabees, 2 Esdras /
-- 4 Ezra), 1 Enoch (`enoch`), Jubilees (`jubilees`). The pseudepigrapha
-- edition is not used at S142 (Matt 12 readings do not surface
-- framework-bearing connections from Testaments of XII / 4 Maccabees /
-- 2 Baruch / 2 Enoch / Adam-Eve at the rigour the migration requires
-- beyond what the apocrypha / 1 Enoch / Jubilees threads already
-- carry). Sonnini''s Acts of Paul, Ascension of Isaiah, Apocalypse of
-- Abraham, and Adam-Eve Conflict do not surface framework-bearing
-- Matt 12 connections at S142. Historical-witness editions (Josephus,
-- M.R. James''s apocryphal NT, Lightfoot''s Apostolic Fathers) remain
-- deferred from V1 cross-refs per the historical-witness one-way rule.
-- The lookup view retains the full S139 edition set for forward
-- compatibility.
--
-- Eleven PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1.  `shabbat-as-covenant-sign-protected-day-and-life-saving-defense`            (sort 271)
--   2.  `mercy-as-true-offering-alms-deliver-from-death-in-sirach-and-tobit`        (sort 272)
--   3.  `eschatological-reversal-righteous-stands-before-those-who-condemned-him`   (sort 273)
--   4.  `spirit-anointed-elect-one-the-spirit-of-wisdom-on-the-son-in-1-enoch`      (sort 274)
--   5.  `compassion-on-the-bruised-cry-of-the-widow-and-orphan-in-sirach`           (sort 275)
--   6.  `binding-of-the-watchers-typological-anchor-for-binding-the-strong-man`     (sort 276)
--   7.  `no-forgiveness-for-the-hardened-disposition-in-jubilees-and-1-enoch-and-wisdom` (sort 277)
--   8.  `tongue-as-trial-of-the-heart-words-as-fruit-of-the-tree-in-sirach-27`      (sort 278)
--   9.  `resurrection-from-sheol-gates-of-the-dead-give-back-in-wisdom-and-1-enoch` (sort 279)
--   10. `adam-and-the-inherited-evil-heart-needing-the-new-heart-cleansing`         (sort 280)
--   11. `children-of-elohim-by-doing-the-fathers-will-in-wisdom-and-sirach-and-jubilees` (sort 281)
--
-- 36 new cross_references rows at tier_required='extras' (Library tier,
-- $4.99) + 11 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required='complete_study'
-- (Companion tier, $9.99). The tier split honors the two-layer
-- architecture of the chapter-end card: Layer 1 (per-verse cross-refs)
-- visible to Library readers who have access to the extras-library
-- editions the refs point to; Layer 2 (framework thread callouts with
-- summary_md + member_notes) gated at Companion, since the threads ARE
-- the framework''s reading of how canon and library answer each other —
-- the "hidden detail expand" that is the Companion-tier upgrade. Every
-- member-note passes the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial
-- checklist. Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el,
-- Ya''aqov, Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Ya''ir, Sha''ul, etc.) are escaped per
-- SQL single-quoted-string-literal convention (every internal '
-- doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 142 — Matt 12 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S140 view including
-- `sonnini-acts-29`; retained for forward compatibility even though
-- Matt 12 does not surface a Sonnini Acts 29 connection at S142.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s142_verse_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 36 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1: shabbat-as-covenant-sign-protected-day-and-life-saving-defense
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 8, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 2, 17,
   '*And He gave us a great sign, the Shabbat day, that we should work six days, but keep Shabbat on the seventh day from all work.* Jubilees 2:17 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Shabbat as the great-sign of the covenant — the same Shabbat-substance Exodus 31:13 names as the *sign between me and the children of Yashar''el (Israel) for ever* and the same substance the King names at Matt 12:8 when he calls himself the *Lord even of the Shabbat day.* The Lord-of-the-Shabbat is the Owner-and-Definer of the covenant-sign he himself gave through Mosheh (Moses); he preserves the sign, he does not abolish it. The wisdom-stream''s sign-of-the-covenant Shabbat-architecture is the substance the King defends against the Pharisaic-fence-architecture at the grain-fields.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 8, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 2, 21,
   '*And He made therein a sign in which they should keep Shabbat with us on the seventh day, to eat and to drink, and to bless Him who hath created all things.* Jubilees 2:21 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Shabbat as the day-of-eating-and-drinking-and-blessing — explicitly the opposite of the fence-architecture that read the Shabbat as restrictive-against-eating-by-plucking-the-Torah-permitted-ears. The wisdom-stream knew the Shabbat as the day-of-eating-and-blessing-the-Creator; the King at Matt 12:1-8 defends the disciples'' plucking-and-eating against the fence-architecture that had inverted the day''s substance. The Jubilees-witness predates the Pharisaic-takkanot and preserves the heart-Shabbat-substance.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 12, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 50, 12,
   '*And the man who does any work thereon, or goes a journey, or tills (his) farm, whether in his house or any other place, and whoever lights a fire, or rides on any beast, or travels by ship on the sea, and whoever strikes or kills anything, or slaughters a beast or a bird, or whoever catches an animal or a bird or a fish, or whoever fasts or makes war on the Shabbats — the man who does any of these things on the Shabbat shall die.* Jubilees 50:12 names the late-Jubilees Shabbat-prohibition code — the wisdom-stream''s most stringent Shabbat-law expression. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:11-12''s *what man shall there be among you, that shall have one sheep, and if it fall into a pit on the Shabbat day, will he not lay hold on it, and lift it out? How much then is a man better than a sheep? Wherefore it is lawful to do well on the Shabbat days.* The wisdom-stream''s strictness on Shabbat-work was the Second-Temple-period architecture the Pharisaic-fence inherited and intensified; the King at Matt 12:12 restores the heart-Shabbat-substance against both Jubilees-stringency-overlay and Pharisaic-fence-architecture — *it is lawful to do well on the Shabbat days,* not by abolishing the Shabbat-keeping but by restoring the day-of-mercy substance that life-saving and doing-well operate within.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 12, 'apocrypha', '1-maccabees', 2, 41,
   '*Then said they every one to his neighbour: If we all do as our brethren have done, and fight not for our lives and laws against the heathen, they will now quickly root us out of the earth. At that time therefore they decreed, saying, Whosoever shall come to make battle with us on the Shabbat day, we will fight against him; neither will we die all, as our brethren that were murdered in the secret places.* 1 Maccabees 2:41 names the Maccabean Shabbat-defense decision — the wisdom-stream''s direct documentation that life-saving-overrides-Shabbat-restriction was the operative-principle in the Second-Temple period. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:11-12: the King''s *kal vachomer* argument (sheep-rescue-on-Shabbat is permitted in the Pharisaic tradition; how much more a man?) walks the same architecture the Hasmonean decision had locked under threat of extinction. The wisdom-stream had named the principle; the King at Matt 12:12 names the operative-substance: the Shabbat is FOR life and rest and doing-well, not for the fence-architecture that obstructs the same.'),

  -- Thread 2: mercy-as-true-offering-alms-deliver-from-death-in-sirach-and-tobit
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 7, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 35, 1,
   '*He that keepeth the law bringeth offerings enough: he that taketh heed to the commandment offereth a peace offering.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 35:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the mercy-substance-IS-the-true-sacrifice architecture: the keeping-of-the-law brings offerings enough; the heeding-of-the-commandment offers the peace offering. The framework reads the verse as the wisdom-stream restatement of Hosea 6:6''s *I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of Elohim (God) more than burnt offerings* — the same architecture Yahusha (Jesus) cites at Matt 12:7 (the second Hosea 6:6 citation in Matthew, after Matt 9:13). The Pharisaic-counterfeit-righteousness fails at the same diagnostic the wisdom-stream had named: external-credential-architecture without internal-mercy-substance is not the offering Yahuah (God) desires.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 7, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 34, 18,
   '*If a man offereth a sacrifice of a thing wrongfully gotten, his offering is ridiculous, and the gifts of unjust men are not accepted.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 34:18 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the heart-substance-required-for-the-sacrifice-to-be-accepted architecture: a sacrifice without the heart-substance is rejected. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:7''s *if ye had known what this meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice, ye would not have condemned the guiltless* — the Pharisees who condemned the disciples for the Shabbat-plucking operated the credential-without-substance pattern Sirach 34:18 had diagnosed: the credentialing-form (Shabbat-fence-adherence) without the mercy-substance is the rejected-offering at the wisdom-stream register.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 7, 'apocrypha', 'tobit', 4, 10,
   '*For alms doth deliver from death, and shall not suffer thee to come into darkness.* Tobit 4:10 names THE strongest wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the mercy-as-substance-with-eternal-weight architecture: alms (the operative-form of the mercy-substance) deliver from death. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:7''s deployment of Hosea 6:6 in the Shabbat-controversy: the mercy-substance is not a soft-side of the Torah; it is the operative-substance with eternal-weight the wisdom-stream had named explicitly. The King at Matt 12:7 names the same operative-substance the wisdom-stream had named — and the Pharisaic-condemnation of the disciples reveals the system''s loss of the substance the wisdom-stream had preserved.'),

  -- Thread 3: eschatological-reversal-righteous-stands-before-those-who-condemned-him
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 14, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 5, 1,
   '*Then shall the righteous man stand in great boldness before the face of such as have afflicted him, and made no account of his labours.* Wisdom of Solomon 5:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the eschatological-reversal-of-the-righteous-condemned architecture: the righteous-one whom the system condemned stands at the day-of-judgment in great-boldness before those-who-afflicted-him. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:14''s Pharisaic-council-to-destroy-the-King: the system''s trajectory from challenging the disciples (Matt 9:11) to slandering the King (Matt 11:18-19) to plotting destruction (Matt 12:14) is the operative-form of the architecture Wisdom 5:1 had named at the eschatological-end-point register. The day-of-judgment reverses the verdict the system rendered in the present age. The King at Matt 12:14 walks toward the cross under the same architecture Wisdom 5 had named at the wisdom-stream register; the resurrection is the operative-vindication.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 14, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 5, 4,
   '*We fools accounted his life madness, and his end to be without honour: How is he numbered among the children of Elohim (God), and his lot is among the saints!* Wisdom of Solomon 5:4-5 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the system''s-belated-recognition-of-the-righteous-one architecture: the same system that accounted his life madness and his end without honour recognizes at the day-of-judgment that he is numbered among the children-of-Elohim (God). The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:14''s council-to-destroy: the Pharisees who plot the King''s destruction will at the day-of-judgment recognize the substance Wisdom 5:4-5 had named — the same architecture operates against the heart-Torah-walking kingdom-citizens of the present age, with the same eschatological-reversal awaiting.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 14, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 95, 7,
   '*Woe to you, sinners, who persecute the righteous; For you will be delivered up and persecuted because of injustice, And heavy will be its yoke upon you.* 1 Enoch 95:7 names the wisdom-stream''s direct woe-against-the-persecutors-of-the-righteous architecture: the same architecture Matt 23 will name in extended form. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:14: the Pharisaic-system''s plot-to-destroy is the operative-action that brings the woe 1 Enoch 95 had named at the wisdom-stream register. The yoke-of-injustice will be heavy upon the persecutors; the kingdom-citizens carry the King''s easy-yoke (Matt 11:30) by contrast. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture''s eschatological-end-point; Matt 12:14 names the inaugural-step that triggers it.'),

  -- Thread 4: spirit-anointed-elect-one-the-spirit-of-wisdom-on-the-son-in-1-enoch
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 18, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 49, 1,
   '*For wisdom is poured out like water, And glory faileth not before him for evermore. For he is mighty in all the secrets of righteousness, And unrighteousness shall disappear as a shadow.* 1 Enoch 49:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the wisdom-poured-out-on-the-Elect-One architecture. Matt 12:18''s *I will put my spirit upon him, and he shall shew judgment to the goyim* (citing Isaiah 42:1) walks the same architecture at the gospel-restatement register: the Father''s-Spirit-anointing of the Son the King walks publicly through the Galilean-ministry. The framework reads the verse-pair as one architecture across two registers: the wisdom-stream knew the Elect-One''s wisdom-anointing-from-the-Father; Matt 12:18 names the operative-fact at the inaugurated-ministry.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 18, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 49, 3,
   '*And in him dwells the spirit of wisdom, And the spirit which gives insight, And the spirit of understanding and of might, And the spirit of those who have fallen asleep in righteousness.* 1 Enoch 49:3 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the four-spirits-on-the-Elect-One architecture — the same four-spirits-cluster Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 11:2 names of the Branch-from-Yishai (Jesse): the spirit of wisdom and understanding, the spirit of counsel and might, the spirit of knowledge and of the fear of Yahuah (the LORD). The framework reads 1 Enoch 49:3 as the wisdom-stream restatement of Isaiah 11:2 applied to the Elect-One — the same Spirit-anointing substance Matt 12:18 names in Yahusha (Jesus) at the immersion (Matt 3:16-17). The Tanakh anchor, the wisdom-stream anchor, and the gospel-fulfillment name one Spirit-anointing-architecture across three registers.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 18, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 62, 2,
   '*And the Lord of Spirits seated him on the throne of His glory, And the spirit of righteousness was poured out upon him, And the word of his mouth slays all the sinners, And all the unrighteous are destroyed from before his face.* 1 Enoch 62:2 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Elect-One enthroned with the spirit-of-righteousness poured out upon him and the word-of-his-mouth as the operative-instrument at the day-of-judgment. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:18-21''s servant-citation read in light of Matt 12:20c (*till he send forth judgment unto victory*): the present-age ministry stages the credentialing-in-mercy-substance; the eschatological-consummation lands the judgment-unto-victory at the second coming. The wisdom-stream knew the Elect-One''s enthronement and the word-as-judgment-instrument; Matt 12:18-21 names the inaugural-credentialing in the meek-King-disposition that precedes the enthronement.'),

  -- Thread 5: compassion-on-the-bruised-cry-of-the-widow-and-orphan-in-sirach
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 20, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 4, 1,
   '*My son, defraud not the poor of his living, and make not the needy eyes to wait long. Make not an hungry soul sorrowful; neither provoke a man in his distress.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 4:1-2 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the bruised-reed-not-broken-and-smoking-flax-not-quenched mercy-substance: the wisdom-stream commands against making-the-needy-wait, against the hungry-soul-sorrowful, against provoking-the-man-in-distress. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:20: *a bruised reed shall he not break, and smoking flax shall he not quench.* The mercy-substance the prophet names of the King is the same substance the wisdom-stream named as the disposition required of the kingdom-citizens. The Pharisaic-system''s pattern of categorical-classification-and-dismissal of the bruised and the smoking inverts both the wisdom-stream-disposition and the King''s-disposition; the King restores; the system breaks-and-snuffs.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 20, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 4, 4,
   '*Reject not the supplication of the afflicted; neither turn away thy face from a poor man. Turn not away thine eye from the needy, and give him none occasion to curse thee.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 4:4-5 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the kingdom-citizens'' compassion-disposition: do not reject-the-supplication, do not turn-the-face-away, do not turn-the-eye-from-the-needy. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:20''s bruised-reed-mercy substance: the disposition of the King walks the wisdom-stream-disposition the Pharisaic-system had abandoned through the categorical-classification-and-dismissal pattern. The wisdom-stream and the gospel name one disposition at two registers.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 20, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 35, 13,
   '*He will not despise the supplication of the fatherless; nor the widow, when she poureth out her complaint. Do not the tears run down the widow''s cheek? and is not her cry against him that causeth them to fall?* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 35:13-14 names THE strongest wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the cry-of-the-bruised-heard-by-Yahuah (God) architecture: he-will-not-despise the supplication of the fatherless and the widow; the cry against the one who causes the tears reaches Yahuah (God). The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:20''s bruised-reed-mercy substance: the wisdom-stream knew Yahuah (God) does not despise the bruised; the King at Matt 12:20 names the operative-disposition in his own ministry. The Pharisaic-system''s plot at v.14 is precisely the act-causing-the-tears the wisdom-stream had named; the King''s mercy-substance at v.20 is the operative-opposite-disposition.'),

  -- Thread 6: binding-of-the-watchers-typological-anchor-for-binding-the-strong-man
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 29, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 10, 4,
   '*And again Yahuah (the Lord) said to Raphael: Bind Azazel hand and foot, and cast him into the darkness: and make an opening in the desert, which is in Dudael, and cast him therein. And place upon him rough and jagged rocks, and cover him with darkness, and let him abide there for ever.* 1 Enoch 10:4-5 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the binding-of-the-watchers-leader-Azazel architecture: bound-hand-and-foot, cast-into-the-darkness, sealed-with-rocks, covered-with-darkness for the appointed-time. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:29''s *how can one enter into a strong man''s house, and spoil his goods, except he first bind the strong man? and then he will spoil his house.* The King''s exorcisms-and-spoiling are the inaugurated-form of the binding-architecture the wisdom-stream had named at the watcher-leader register; the full-binding-of-Satan at Revelation 20:1-3 lands the architecture at the millennial-consummation. The wisdom-stream knew the binding-and-darkness-and-appointed-time pattern; the King at Matt 12:29 walks the inaugurated-binding-and-spoiling.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 29, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 54, 5,
   '*And I asked the angel of peace who went with me, saying: For whom are these chains being prepared? And he said unto me: These are being prepared for the hosts of Azazel, so that they may take them and cast them into the abyss of complete condemnation, and they shall cover their jaws with rough stones as Yahuah (the Lord) of Spirits commanded.* 1 Enoch 54:5 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the chains-prepared-for-Azazel-and-his-hosts and the casting-into-the-abyss-of-complete-condemnation architecture. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:29''s binding-the-strong-man: the wisdom-stream knew the chains-prepared and the abyss-of-condemnation as the eschatological-architecture awaiting Azazel and his hosts; the King at Matt 12:29 walks the inaugurated-action that culminates in the architecture the wisdom-stream had named.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 29, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 10, 11,
   '*And one of us he commanded that we should teach Noah all their medicines; for he knew that they would not walk in uprightness, nor strive in righteousness. And we did according to all his words: all the malignant evil ones we bound in the place of condemnation, and a tenth part of them we left to be subject before Satan on the earth.* Jubilees 10:9-11 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the watchers-bound-with-a-tenth-permitted-to-operate architecture: nine-tenths bound in the place-of-condemnation, one-tenth permitted before Satan on the earth. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:29''s binding-the-strong-man: the wisdom-stream knew the partial-binding-with-a-remnant-operating architecture; the King at Matt 12:29 walks the inaugurated-completion of the binding-arc that culminates in Revelation 20:1-3''s thousand-year-binding and the brief-final-loosing.'),

  -- Thread 7: no-forgiveness-for-the-hardened-disposition-in-jubilees-and-1-enoch-and-wisdom
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 31, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 15, 33,
   '*And yet they will make their sons after the manner of the Gentiles in all their pollutions and uncleanness, and there will not be left a son of the covenant, nor a son of the covenant who is pure, but he will profane himself with every kind of pollution. And great wrath from Yahuah (the Lord) will be upon the children of Yashar''el (Israel), because they have forsaken His covenant and have turned aside from His word.* Jubilees 15:33-34 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the great-wrath-no-forgiveness for the deliberate-covenant-rejection architecture. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:31-32''s blasphemy-against-the-Ruach: the deliberate-attribution of the Ruach''s-work to demonic-agency by those who have seen the credentialing-clearly is the same deliberate-rejection-of-the-covenant the wisdom-stream had named at Jubilees 15:33-34. The seriousness Jubilees names of the wrath-against-the-deliberate-rejector is the substance Matt 12:32''s *neither in this world, neither in the world to come* carries.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 32, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 65, 11,
   '*And he answered and said unto me: They have witnessed those that have been guilty of the offence of their sin, and they have rejected its sentence: and they have practised the works which the watchers of heaven have taught — and they have no honour before Yahuah (the Lord); and they shall not have any rest: that is the appointed time for them and there is no place of repentance for them.* 1 Enoch 65:11 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the no-place-of-repentance architecture: those who have witnessed-the-sin and rejected-the-sentence and practiced-the-works-of-the-watchers have no-place-of-repentance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:32: the deliberate-attribution of the Ruach''s-work to demonic-agency is the witnessing-and-rejecting-the-sentence pattern the wisdom-stream had named — the disposition hardened against correction with no repentance remaining. The Pharisaic-attribution Yahusha (Jesus) is responding to IS the diagnostic-instance of the architecture 1 Enoch 65:11 had named at its terminus.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 32, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 12, 10,
   '*But executing thy judgments upon them by little and little, thou gavest them place of repentance, not being ignorant that they were a naughty generation, and that their malice was bred in them, and that their cogitation would never be changed.* Wisdom of Solomon 12:10 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the architecture-of-the-hardened-disposition that-will-never-be-changed: Yahuah (God) gives place of repentance, not being ignorant of the bred-in malice and the cogitation that will never change. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:31-32''s blasphemy-against-the-Ruach: the wisdom-stream knew the hardened-disposition that will never change as a possibility-of-the-heart; the King at Matt 12:31-32 names the architecture''s consequence — the blasphemy of those whose cogitation has hardened against the credentialing they have seen will not be forgiven, because the disposition itself is the hardening-against-repentance the wisdom-stream had named.'),

  -- Thread 8: tongue-as-trial-of-the-heart-words-as-fruit-of-the-tree-in-sirach-27
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 34, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 27, 6,
   '*The fruit declareth if the tree have been dressed; so is the utterance of a conceit in the heart of man.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 27:6 names THE strongest wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for Matt 12:33-35''s tree-known-by-its-fruit / out-of-the-abundance-of-the-heart-the-mouth-speaketh architecture: the fruit-declares-the-tree''s-dressing; the utterance-declares-the-heart''s-conceit. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture in precisely the substance the King walks at Matt 12:33-35. *O generation of vipers, how can ye, being evil, speak good things? for out of the abundance of the heart the mouth speaketh* (Matt 12:34) names the same diagnostic Sirach 27:6 had named: words-are-fruit-of-the-heart; bad-fruit-reveals-bad-heart-substance.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 36, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 27, 7,
   '*Praise no man before thou hearest him speak; for this is the trial of men.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 27:7 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of speech-as-the-trial-of-men architecture: hear-the-man-speak-first-because-this-is-the-trial. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:36''s *every idle word that men shall speak, they shall give account thereof in the day of judgment* — the day-of-judgment is the cosmic-version of the wisdom-stream''s speech-as-trial architecture: the words-spoken are the evidence-of-the-heart-substance the judgment will weigh.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 36, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 1, 11,
   '*Therefore beware of murmuring, which is unprofitable; and refrain your tongue from backbiting: for there is no word so secret, that shall go for nought: and the mouth that belieth slayeth the soul.* Wisdom of Solomon 1:11 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the no-word-goes-for-nought-and-the-mouth-that-belieth-slays-the-soul architecture: words have eternal-weight at the wisdom-stream register; the lying mouth slays the soul. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:36''s *every idle word ... give account thereof in the day of judgment*: the wisdom-stream had named the architecture the King names at the day-of-judgment register. *By thy words thou shalt be justified, and by thy words thou shalt be condemned* (Matt 12:37) walks the same architecture: words-as-evidence-of-the-heart-substance the day-of-judgment will weigh.'),

  -- Thread 9: resurrection-from-sheol-gates-of-the-dead-give-back-in-wisdom-and-1-enoch
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 40, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 16, 13,
   '*For thou hast power of life and death: thou leadest to the gates of Sheol, and bringest up again.* Wisdom of Solomon 16:13 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the gates-of-Sheol-and-bring-up-again architecture: Yahuah (God) has the power of life and death; he leads to the gates of Sheol AND brings up again. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:40''s *so shall the Son of Adam be three days and three nights in the heart of the earth* — the sign-of-Yonah''s three-days-three-nights-in-the-heart-of-the-earth is the operative-application of the architecture Wisdom 16:13 had named: descent-to-Sheol-and-bring-up-again. The wisdom-stream knew Yahuah (God) brings up from Sheol; the King''s resurrection is the credentialing-event the typology pre-announces.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 40, 'enoch', '1-enoch', 51, 1,
   '*And in those days shall the earth also give back that which has been entrusted to it, And Sheol also shall give back that which it has received, And hell shall give back that which it owes.* 1 Enoch 51:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the earth-and-Sheol-and-hell-giving-back-what-they-have-received architecture: resurrection-from-the-place-of-the-dead at the appointed-time. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:40''s sign-of-Yonah three-days-and-three-nights-in-the-heart-of-the-earth: the wisdom-stream knew the earth-and-Sheol-giving-back-the-dead architecture; the King at Matt 12:40 names the inaugurated-form of the architecture in his own future-resurrection that the Yonah-typology pre-announces. The Yonah-vomited-out-by-the-fish at Yonah (Jonah) 2:10 is the typological-anchor the King draws; the wisdom-stream architecture of Sheol-giving-back is the framework-context.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 40, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 23, 30,
   '*And at that time Yahuah (the Lord) will heal His servants, And they shall rise up and see great peace, And drive out their adversaries.* Jubilees 23:30 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the rise-up-and-see-great-peace architecture: the servants-of-Yahuah (God) rise up at the appointed-time. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:40''s sign-of-Yonah resurrection-pre-announcement: the wisdom-stream knew the rising-up-of-the-servants as the latter-day-architecture; the King''s own resurrection at the appointed-time is the inaugurated-credentialing of the architecture the wisdom-stream had named.'),

  -- Thread 10: adam-and-the-inherited-evil-heart-needing-the-new-heart-cleansing
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 45, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 48,
   '*O Adam, what hast thou done? for though it was thou that sinned, thou art not fallen alone, but we all that come of thee. For what doth this also profit, that we should now be promised an immortal time, whereas we have done the works that bring death?* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:48 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Adam-introduced-the-evil-heart-and-the-children-inherit-it architecture: Adam''s sin is not Adam''s alone; the children-of-Adam inherit the operative-pattern. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:43-45''s empty-house parable: the cleansed-house empty-of-the-new-heart is precisely the architecture 2 Esdras 7:48 had named — the children-of-Adam without the new-heart-cleansing carry the inherited-pattern that produces the empty-house-vulnerability. The wisdom-stream knew the architecture of the inherited-evil-heart; the King''s empty-house parable names the architecture''s operative-form at the deliverance-without-internal-replacement register.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 45, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 7, 118,
   '*O thou Adam, what hast thou done? for though it was thou that sinned, thou art not fallen alone, but we all that come of thee.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 7:118 names the wisdom-stream''s direct restatement of the Adam-and-the-children-of-Adam architecture — the same wisdom-stream witness Augustine later wove into the inherited-original-sin doctrine. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:45''s *the last state of that man is worse than the first:* the architecture is the empty-house-vulnerability without the new-heart-substance; the children-of-Adam without internal-substance are exactly what the empty-house parable diagnoses. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture; the King''s parable names its operative-consequence.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 45, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 1, 23,
   '*And after this they will turn to Me in all uprightness and with all (their) heart and with all (their) soul, and I shall circumcise the foreskin of their heart and the foreskin of the heart of their seed, and I shall create in them a holy spirit, and I shall cleanse them so that they shall not turn away from Me from that day unto eternity.* Jubilees 1:23 names the wisdom-stream''s direct Tanakh-anchor parallel to Yirmeyahu (Jeremiah) 31:33 and Yechezk''el (Ezekiel) 36:26-27: the new-heart-circumcision and the holy-spirit-creation and the cleansing-that-does-not-turn-away. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:43-45''s empty-house parable: the cleansed-house empty-of-the-new-heart is the architecture the parable diagnoses; Jubilees 1:23''s new-heart-and-holy-spirit-and-cleansing is the internal-replacement the deliverance-process requires. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture''s positive-substance; the King''s parable names the architecture''s negative-correlate — the deliverance-without-the-internal-replacement Jubilees 1:23 names is the empty-house Matt 12:43-45 walks.'),

  -- Thread 11: children-of-elohim-by-doing-the-fathers-will-in-wisdom-and-sirach-and-jubilees
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 50, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 13,
   '*He professeth to have the knowledge of Elohim (God): and he calleth himself the child of Yahuah (the Lord). He was made to reprove our thoughts. He is grievous unto us even to behold: for his life is not like other men''s, his ways are of another fashion.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:13-15 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the child-of-Elohim-by-the-righteous-disposition architecture: the righteous-one calls-himself-the-child-of-Yahuah (the Lord) by his life-of-another-fashion (the heart-Torah-walking life). The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:50''s *whosoever shall do the will of my Father which is in heaven, the same is my brother, and sister, and mother* — the kingdom-family-recognition-criterion is the same doing-the-Father''s-will substance the wisdom-stream had named as the operative-form of the child-of-Yahuah (the Lord) identity. The wisdom-stream knew the architecture; the King at Matt 12:50 names the kingdom-family substance.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 50, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 18,
   '*For if the just man be the son of Elohim (God), he will help him, and deliver him from the hand of his enemies.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:18 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the son-of-Elohim-tested-by-deliverance architecture: the just-man''s son-of-Elohim-identity is to be tested by whether Yahuah (God) helps him. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:50''s kingdom-family-recognition-criterion: the doing-the-Father''s-will substance is the operative-identity-marker — the system''s test (Wisdom 2:18) is whether Yahuah (God) delivers; the King''s test (Matt 12:50) is whether the heart walks the will of the Father. The same architecture from both sides: the heart-Torah-walking-life IS the son-of-Elohim-identity-marker at both registers.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 50, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 4, 10,
   '*Be as a father unto the fatherless, and instead of an husband unto their mother: so shalt thou be as the son of the most High, and he shall love thee more than thy mother doth.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 4:10 names THE strongest wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the doing-the-Father''s-substance-makes-thee-a-son-of-the-Most-High architecture: the disposition-of-fathering-the-fatherless and being-a-husband-to-their-mother makes the doer the son-of-the-Most-High. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:50: the kingdom-family-recognition-criterion is the same doing-the-Father''s-will substance the wisdom-stream had named as the operative-form of the son-of-the-Most-High identity. The wisdom-stream and the gospel name one architecture across two registers — the kingdom-family is identified by the heart-Torah-walking-disposition the wisdom-stream had named, the kingdom-entry-criterion at Matt 7:21 had named, and the 1 John 2:3-4 master-filter restates.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 12, 50, 'jubilees', 'jubilees', 1, 24,
   '*And their souls will cleave to Me and to all My commandments, and they will fulfil My commandments, and I shall be their Father and they will be My children.* Jubilees 1:24 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the souls-cleaving-to-Yahuah-and-fulfilling-the-commandments yields the Father-and-children-relation architecture. The framework reads the verse against Matt 12:50''s kingdom-family-recognition-criterion: the doing-of-the-Father''s-will substance is the operative-form of the fulfilling-of-the-commandments Jubilees 1:24 names. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture explicitly in covenant-and-commandment language; the King at Matt 12:50 names the same architecture in kingdom-family-recognition language. The kingdom-family is identified by the same standard the 1 John 2:3-4 master-filter restates: *if we keep his commandments.*')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s142_verse_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug = i.src_edition
                            AND sv.book_slug    = i.src_slug
                            AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                            AND sv.verse_number  = i.src_v
  JOIN _s142_verse_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug = i.tgt_edition
                            AND tv.book_slug    = i.tgt_slug
                            AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                            AND tv.verse_number  = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

